<script>(function(){var P=[["Battle of the Trebia","/battle/battle-of-the-trebia","Battle","22 or 23 December 218 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army lured a Roman army under the consul Sempronius Longus across the icy Trebia near Placentia in December 218 BCE, in the first major battle of the Second Punic War, and defeated it heavily."],["Battles of Khalkhin Gol","/battle/battles-of-khalkhin-gol","Battle","11 May – 15 September 1939","Soviet and Mongolian forces under Georgy Zhukov fought Japanese and Manchukoan forces on the disputed Mongolia-Manchukuo border in 1939, and by 31 August had trapped and destroyed the Japanese forces on the Mongolian side."],["Battle of Alarcos","/battle/battle-of-alarcos","Battle","18 July 1195","The Almohad caliph Abu Yusuf Ya'qub al-Mansur defeated King Alfonso VIII of Castile at Alarcos, near the Guadiana, on 18 July 1195, and Castile's field army was destroyed, leaving the road to Toledo open."],["Battle of the Catalaunian Plains","/battle/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains","Battle","20 June 451 CE","A coalition led by the Roman general Aetius and the Visigothic king Theodoric I fought the Huns and their vassals under Attila in Gaul in 451 CE; Theodoric was killed, Attila withdrew, and the outcome is disputed."],["Battle of Gettysburg","/battle/battle-of-gettysburg","Battle","1 to 3 July 1863","Union forces under George Meade defeated Robert E. Lee's Confederate army at Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, from 1 to 3 July 1863, ending Lee's invasion of the North and forcing his retreat to Virginia."],["Battles of Lexington and Concord","/battle/battles-of-lexington-and-concord","Battle","19 April 1775","British regulars sent from Boston to seize military supplies at Concord fought Massachusetts militia at Lexington, Concord and along the road back on 19 April 1775, the first major fighting of the American Revolutionary War."],["Battle of Nagashino","/battle/battle-of-nagashino","Battle","29 June 1575","In June 1575 the allied armies of Oda Nobunaga and Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated Takeda Katsuyori's army near Nagashino Castle in Mikawa Province, Japan, killing many Takeda generals and making Nobunaga's unification of Japan seem certain."],["Battle of Raphia","/battle/battle-of-raphia","Battle","22 June 217 BCE","Ptolemy IV of Egypt defeated Antiochus III of the Seleucid Empire near Raphia on 22 June 217 BCE, in the Fourth Syrian War, and kept Coele-Syria for Egypt until Antiochus took it back at Panium in 200 BCE."],["Battle of Actium","/battle/battle-of-actium","Battle","2 September 31 BCE","Octavian's fleet under Marcus Agrippa defeated the combined fleets of Mark Antony and Cleopatra off Actium in the Ionian Sea in 31 BCE, after which both took their own lives and Octavian became sole master of Rome."],["Battle of the Yarmuk","/battle/battle-of-the-yarmuk","Battle","15 to 20 August 636","In August 636 the Rashidun Caliphate's army under Khalid ibn al-Walid defeated a larger Byzantine army under Vahan near the Yarmuk River, which ended Byzantine rule in Syria and opened the way to Egypt."],["Battle of Sagrajas","/battle/battle-of-sagrajas","Battle","23 October 1086","An Almoravid army under Yusuf ibn Tashfin, joined by the taifa kings of al-Andalus, defeated Alfonso VI of Castile near Badajoz in October 1086, easing Christian pressure on the taifas and opening the way for Almoravid rule in al-Andalus."],["Battle of Karbala","/battle/battle-of-karbala","Battle","10 October 680","On 10 October 680 at Karbala in southern Iraq, the army of the Umayyad caliph Yazid I killed Husayn ibn Ali, grandson of Muhammad, and most of his small party, with consequences for the Second Fitna and for Shia identity."],["Battle of Midway","/battle/battle-of-midway","Battle","4–7 June 1942","Two United States carrier groups sank all four Japanese fleet carriers present near Midway Atoll in June 1942, six months after Pearl Harbor, and wrecked Admiral Yamamoto's plan to capture the atoll and destroy the American carriers."],["Battle of Hastings","/battle/battle-of-hastings","Battle","14 October 1066","On 14 October 1066 William, Duke of Normandy, defeated the English army of King Harold Godwinson about 7 miles northwest of Hastings; Harold was killed, and William was crowned king on Christmas Day."],["Battle of Zama","/battle/battle-of-zama","Battle","202 BCE","A Roman army under Scipio Africanus defeated a Carthaginian army under Hannibal near Zama in what is now Tunisia in 202 BCE, ending the Second Punic War and leaving Carthage politically subordinate to Rome."],["Third Battle of Panipat","/battle/third-battle-of-panipat","Battle","14 January 1761","On 14 January 1761 the Durrani Empire and its Indian allies defeated the Maratha army at Panipat, 97 kilometres north of Delhi; tens of thousands of Marathas died in the fighting and after it."],["Battle of Kadesh","/battle/battle-of-kadesh","Battle","May 1274 BCE","Ramesses II of Egypt and Muwatalli II of the Hittite Empire fought on the Orontes near Kadesh after a Hittite attack nearly broke the Egyptian army; both sides claimed victory and the Hittites kept Kadesh."],["Battle of Navarino","/battle/battle-of-navarino","Battle","20 October 1827","A British, French and Russian fleet under Admiral Codrington defeated and largely destroyed an Ottoman and Egyptian fleet at anchor in Navarino Bay in 1827, during the Greek War of Independence, which made Greek independence much more likely."],["Battle of Carrhae","/battle/battle-of-carrhae","Battle","9 June 53 BCE","A Parthian cavalry army under Surena defeated the Roman army of Marcus Licinius Crassus near Carrhae in 53 BCE; Crassus was killed, most of his men were killed or captured, and Parthia later invaded Syria and Armenia."],["Battle of Boyacá","/battle/battle-of-boyaca","Battle","7 August 1819","A combined Venezuelan and New Granadan army with a British Legion under Simón Bolívar defeated Colonel José María Barreiro's Spanish III Division at Boyacá in 1819, opening the road to Santa Fe and the founding of Gran Colombia."],["Battle of the Teutoburg Forest","/battle/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest","Battle","8 to 11 September 9 CE","An alliance of Germanic peoples led by Arminius ambushed three Roman legions under Publius Quinctilius Varus in 9 CE, possibly near Kalkriese, and ended Roman expansion beyond the Rhine."],["Battle of Jutland","/battle/battle-of-jutland","Battle","31 May – 1 June 1916","The British Grand Fleet under Jellicoe and the German High Seas Fleet under Scheer fought off the Danish coast of Jutland in 1916; Britain lost more ships and men, but the German fleet returned to port and stayed there."],["Battle of Poltava","/battle/battle-of-poltava","Battle","8 July 1709","A Russian army under Tsar Peter I defeated a Swedish army commanded by Carl Gustaf Rehnskiöld near Poltava in Ukraine on 8 July 1709, the largest battle of the Great Northern War; the rest of the Swedish army surrendered three days later."],["Battle of Vienna (1683)","/battle/battle-of-vienna-1683","Battle","12 September 1683","On 12 September 1683 a relief army of Imperial and Polish forces under John III Sobieski defeated the Ottoman army of Kara Mustafa Pasha at Vienna, after a two-month siege, and the Ottomans were later driven from most of Hungary."],["Battle of the Hydaspes","/battle/battle-of-the-hydaspes","Battle","May 326 BCE","Alexander the Great's Macedonian army crossed the swollen Hydaspes in May 326 BCE and defeated the Pauravas under Porus on its bank in what is now Punjab, Pakistan; Alexander spared Porus and made him a satrap."],["Battle of Dien Bien Phu","/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu","Battle","13 March – 7 May 1954","Viet Minh forces under Võ Nguyên Giáp besieged and overran a French Union garrison in the valley of Điện Biên Phủ in northwest Tonkin in 1954, in the First Indochina War, and French withdrawal from Indochina followed."],["Battle of Stalingrad","/battle/battle-of-stalingrad","Battle","17 July 1942 – 2 February 1943","The Soviet Union defeated Germany and its Axis allies at Stalingrad on the Volga between 1942 and 1943; the German 6th Army was encircled and surrendered, and the strategic initiative on the Eastern Front passed to the Red Army."],["Battle of Uhud","/battle/battle-of-uhud","Battle","23 March 625","The Quraysh of Mecca under Abu Sufyan ibn Harb fought the early Muslims under Muhammad near Mount Uhud, north of Medina, in March 625; the Muslims lost heavily after part of their archer force left its hill, and the Meccans withdrew without pressing on."],["Battle of Guandu","/battle/battle-of-guandu","Battle","200 CE","In 200 CE, late in the Eastern Han dynasty, the warlord Cao Cao held the fortified camp at Guandu against the larger army of Yuan Shao, burned Yuan's grain at Wuchao and routed him, becoming the dominant power in northern China."],["Battle of Badr","/battle/battle-of-badr","Battle","13 March 624 CE","On 13 March 624 CE (17 Ramadan, 2 AH) Muhammad's followers from Medina defeated a larger Qurayshi army from Mecca near Badr, killing several Meccan leaders and strengthening Muhammad's position."],["Battle of Kosovo","/battle/battle-of-kosovo","Battle","15 June 1389","An Ottoman army under Sultan Murad I fought an army led by the Serbian Prince Lazar Hrebeljanović on the Kosovo field in 1389; both leaders died, both armies were badly weakened, and the Serbian principalities later became Ottoman vassals."],["Battle of Trafalgar","/battle/battle-of-trafalgar","Battle","21 October 1805","A British fleet under Vice-Admiral Nelson defeated a combined French and Spanish fleet under Villeneuve off Cape Trafalgar in 1805, losing no ship, though Nelson was killed; Britain's command of the sea was not tested for over a century."],["Second Battle of Panipat","/battle/second-battle-of-panipat","Battle","5 November 1556","On 5 November 1556 the Mughals under the young Akbar and his guardian Bairam Khan defeated Hemchandra Vikramaditya, known as Hemu, at Panipat, after he had taken Delhi and Agra; Hemu was captured and beheaded."],["Battle of Puebla","/battle/battle-of-puebla","Battle","5 May 1862","French troops under Charles de Lorencez failed three times to storm the Mexican forts of Loreto and Guadalupe above Puebla on 5 May 1862, during the second French intervention in Mexico, and withdrew to Orizaba to await reinforcements."],["Battle of the Granicus","/battle/battle-of-the-granicus","Battle","May 334 BCE","In May 334 BCE Alexander the Great of Macedon defeated the field army of the Persian satraps of Asia Minor at the crossing of the Granicus in the Troad, the first of his three major battles with the Achaemenid Empire."],["Battle of Yamen","/battle/battle-of-yamen","Battle","19 March 1279","A Yuan fleet under Zhang Hongfan defeated the chained Song fleet in the bay at Yamen in southern China on 19 March 1279, ending the Song dynasty; the child emperor Zhao Bing died in the sea."],["Battle of Königgrätz","/battle/battle-of-koniggratz","Battle","3 July 1866","On 3 July 1866 the Prussian armies defeated the Austrian army of Ludwig von Benedek near Königgrätz in Bohemia, the decisive battle of the Austro-Prussian War, which cleared the way for a German state without Austria."],["Battle of Agincourt","/battle/battle-of-agincourt","Battle","25 October 1415","On 25 October 1415 Henry V's English army, marching to Calais and heavily outnumbered, defeated a French army near Azincourt in northern France, a victory that gave England the advantage in the Hundred Years' War for some years."],["Battle of Leipzig","/battle/battle-of-leipzig","Battle","16–19 October 1813","The armies of the Sixth Coalition, from Austria, Prussia, Sweden and Russia, defeated Napoleon's Grande Armée at Leipzig in Saxony over four days in October 1813, and the French withdrew to France."],["Battle of Pydna","/battle/battle-of-pydna","Battle","22 June 168 BCE","Roman legions under the consul Lucius Aemilius Paullus defeated King Perseus of Macedon and his phalanx near Pydna in 168 BCE, in the Third Macedonian War, ending the Antigonid line of kings and Macedonian independence."],["Battle of Oriskany","/battle/battle-of-oriskany","Battle","6 August 1777","On 6 August 1777 Loyalists and Britain's Indigenous allies ambushed an American militia column and Oneida warriors under Nicholas Herkimer near Oriska, stopping the relief of Fort Stanwix, though the siege was abandoned two weeks later."],["Battle of Gaugamela","/battle/battle-of-gaugamela","Battle","1 October 331 BCE","Alexander the Great and the army of Macedon defeated the Persian army of Darius III at Gaugamela, north of Arbela in what is now Iraq, in 331 BCE; the Achaemenid Empire fell soon after."],["Battle of the Bulge","/battle/battle-of-the-bulge","Battle","16 December 1944 – 25 January 1945","A German offensive through the Ardennes in Belgium and Luxembourg took the Western Allies by surprise on 16 December 1944 but was halted short of the Meuse, and the front was restored by the end of January 1945."],["Battle of Salamis","/battle/battle-of-salamis","Battle","480 BCE","An Allied Greek fleet under Themistocles defeated a larger Achaemenid fleet under King Xerxes in the straits between the island of Salamis and the mainland in 480 BCE, after which Xerxes withdrew with much of his army."],["Battle of Kohima","/battle/battle-of-kohima","Battle","4 April – 22 June 1944","A British and Indian garrison held Kohima ridge against the Japanese 31st Division in April 1944, was relieved, and with reinforcements drove the Japanese off, reopening the road to Imphal in June."],["Battle of Poitiers (1356)","/battle/battle-of-poitiers-1356","Battle","19 September 1356","An Anglo-Gascon army under Edward, the Black Prince, defeated a larger French army under King John II south of Poitiers in 1356, during the Hundred Years' War, and captured the king, which led to a truce and the Treaty of Brétigny."],["Battle of Issus","/battle/battle-of-issus","Battle","5 November 333 BCE","Alexander the Great's Hellenic League army defeated the Achaemenid army of Darius III near the Pinarus river by Issus in southern Anatolia in 333 BCE, and Darius fled, leaving his family and treasury to be captured."],["Battle of Crécy","/battle/battle-of-crecy","Battle","26 August 1346","An English army under Edward III, standing on a hillside near Crécy-en-Ponthieu in northern France, beat off repeated attacks by a much larger French army under Philip VI in 1346, during the Hundred Years' War, and went on to take Calais."],["Battle of Marathon","/battle/battle-of-marathon","Battle","12 September 490 BCE","The Athenians, helped by Plataea, defeated a Persian force under Datis and Artaphernes on the plain of Marathon in Attica in 490 BCE, ending the first Persian invasion of Greece."],["Battle on the Ice","/battle/battle-on-the-ice","Battle","5 April 1242","The united forces of Novgorod and Vladimir-Suzdal under Prince Alexander Nevsky defeated the Livonian Order and the Bishopric of Dorpat under Bishop Hermann of Dorpat at Lake Peipus on 5 April 1242, a battle later made a Russian national symbol."],["First Battle of the Marne","/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne","Battle","5 to 12 September 1914","French and British armies under Joffre counter-attacked the German right wing between Paris and Verdun in September 1914, forced the Germans to retreat to the Aisne and ended the German plan for a quick victory in the west."],["Fall of Constantinople","/battle/fall-of-constantinople","Battle","6 April to 29 May 1453","The Ottoman army under Sultan Mehmed II besieged Constantinople for 53 days and took the Byzantine capital on 29 May 1453, after which the city was sacked and became the Ottoman capital; the fate of Emperor Constantine XI is unknown."],["Battle of Tsushima","/battle/battle-of-tsushima","Battle","27–28 May 1905","In the Tsushima Strait on 27–28 May 1905 the Japanese Combined Fleet under Tōgō Heihachirō destroyed or captured nearly all of the Russian Second Pacific Squadron under Rozhestvensky, and Russia sued for peace that year."],["Battle of Thermopylae","/battle/battle-of-thermopylae","Battle","480 BCE, between July and September","In 480 BCE a Greek force led by the Spartan king Leonidas I held the pass of Thermopylae for several days against the Persian army of Xerxes, until the Persians found a path behind them and killed the Greek rearguard."],["Battle of San Jacinto","/battle/battle-of-san-jacinto","Battle","21 April 1836","A Texian army under Sam Houston defeated Antonio López de Santa Anna's Mexican force in about 18 minutes at San Jacinto in Texas on 21 April 1836, the last battle of the Texas Revolution, and Santa Anna was captured the next day."],["Battle of Isandlwana","/battle/battle-of-isandlwana","Battle","22 January 1879","A Zulu army of some 20,000 overran part of the British main column at Isandlwana in Zululand on 22 January 1879, early in the Anglo-Zulu War, killing over 1,300 troops and bringing a larger second British invasion."],["Battle of al-Qadisiyyah","/battle/battle-of-al-qadisiyyah","Battle","November 636","In November 636 the army of the Rashidun Caliphate defeated the Sasanian army of Rustam Farrokhzad at al-Qadisiyyah in Iraq, after which Ctesiphon fell and the Sasanians lost Mesopotamia."],["Battle of the Little Bighorn","/battle/battle-of-the-little-bighorn","Battle","25–26 June 1876","On the Little Bighorn River in Montana Territory, Lakota, Northern Cheyenne and Arapaho forces defeated the 7th Cavalry under Lieutenant Colonel Custer in June 1876, the most significant action of the Great Sioux War, which the United States still won."],["Battle of Mohács","/battle/battle-of-mohacs","Battle","29 August 1526","The Ottoman army under Suleiman the Magnificent defeated the Hungarian army of King Louis II near Mohács in 1526; Louis died in flight, and Hungary was later divided between the Ottomans, the Habsburgs and an eastern kingdom."],["Battle of Cannae","/battle/battle-of-cannae","Battle","2 August 216 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army surrounded and destroyed most of a larger Roman and allied army under the consuls Paullus and Varro at Cannae in Apulia in 216 BCE, during the Second Punic War."]],d=Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5),p=P[d%P.length],a=document.getElementById("hub-pick");if(a){a.href=p[1];var im=document.createElement("img");im.src="/logos/thumbs/"+encodeURIComponent(p[0]).replace(/'/g,"%27")+".png";im.alt="";im.width=64;im.height=64;a.querySelector(".hub-pick-img").appendChild(im);a.querySelector(".hub-pick-k").textContent="Today\u2019s pick \u00b7 "+p[2]+(p[3]?" \u00b7 "+p[3]:"");a.querySelector(".hub-pick-n").textContent=p[0];a.querySelector(".hub-pick-d").textContent=p[4];}var b=document.getElementById("hub-surprise"),P=["/battle/"];if(b)b.addEventListener("click",function(){function go(){if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES==="undefined")return;var a=SEARCH_PROFILES.filter(function(r){return P.some(function(p){return r[1].indexOf(p)===0})});if(a.length)location.href=a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)][1]}if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES!=="undefined")return go();var sc=document.createElement("script");sc.src=(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC!=="undefined"?SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC:"/search-profiles.js");sc.onload=go;sc.onerror=go;document.head.appendChild(sc)});})();</script>
